"Rust code must absolutely avoid 'unsafe' and any path that can panic. Never call panicking APIs: no unwrap(), expect(), panic!, unreachable!, todo!, unimplemented!, no indexing/slicing that can panic (use get/get_mut), and no arithmetic that can overflow-panic (use checked_/saturating_). Always prefer a safe alternative: unwrap_or_default, unwrap_or, unwrap_or_else, the ? operator / Result, explicit Option handling. Rationale: a panic aborts a SpacetimeDB reducer and can wedge the module (e.g. a panicking scheduled tick loops forever), so panics are never acceptable, especially in server code."